  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total obligations for small-business federal contractors in FY2026 to date are $20.7B. All figures are contract obligations, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. obligated $2.6B, making it the largest small-business recipient by obligations. AMERICAN CENTRIFUGE OPERATING, LLC obligated $916M, GENERAL MATTER, INC. obligated $900M, and CSI AVIATION, INC obligated $835M. W S DARLEY & CO obligated $829M, FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. obligated $710M, THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC obligated $707M, MINBURN TECHNOLOGY GROUP, LLC obligated $686M, COCHRANE USA INC obligated $641M, and ANDURIL INDUSTRIES, INC. obligated $611M. Rankings list firms by obligations and show concentration at the top: a single firm holds $2.6B of the $20.7B total. Readers should treat these numbers as partial fiscal-year results rather than full-year totals. The list reflects obligations recorded through FY2026 to date and can help contracting officers, industry analysts, and small businesses benchmark where federal dollars have flowed so far this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who leads the FY2026 small-business obligations list?",
        "body": "ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. leads the FY2026 small-business obligations list with $2.6B. AMERICAN CENTRIFUGE OPERATING, LLC and GENERAL MATTER, INC. follow with $916M and $900M respectively. The top ten together account for a substantial share of the $20.7B total obligations for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What should users know about these obligation figures?",
        "body": "All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The ranking reflects obligations recorded through FY2026 to date and is not a full-year summary. Use the list to compare where obligations are concentrated among small businesses so far this fiscal year."
      }
    ]
  },
